cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Risk Management Engine
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Lyonn
    family-names: Lie
    alias: leeyawnnn
repository-code: "https://github.com/leeyawnnn/risk_management_system-"
abstract: >-
  A multi-asset portfolio risk engine in C++20 computing Value at Risk
  by parametric, historical and Monte Carlo methods, Expected Shortfall,
  marginal and component risk attribution, factor risk decomposition,
  forward and reverse stress testing, and the regulatory backtests that
  assess calibration: Kupiec proportion-of-failures, Christoffersen
  independence and conditional coverage, Basel traffic-light zones, and
  the Acerbi-Szekely Expected Shortfall tests. The worked example uses
  real daily series from FRED.
keywords:
  - risk management
  - value at risk
  - expected shortfall
  - quantitative finance
  - portfolio analytics
  - backtesting
  - cpp
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-18"
